<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- RadarSettingsTab — the Radar tab of the Settings window: what the map DRAWS over the basemap for radar.

       ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │  ⌄  Home site                                        │
       │    Home site: KTLX · Norman                          │  ← set in the Radar Atlas, not here
       │                                                      │     (load-on-launch → the Startup tab)
       │  ⌄  Readouts                                         │
       │    Distance  [ km | mi | nm ]                        │  ← PERSISTED, app-wide
       │  ⌄  NowCast live polling                             │
       │    [ Regime-aware | Fixed time ]                     │  ← PERSISTED (RegimeAwarePolling), default
       │    Checks for a new scan when the radar's own …     │     regime-aware; the explainer follows the mode
       │    Check every [ 20 s | 30 s | 45 s | 60 s ]         │  ← PERSISTED (LivePollSeconds); GREYED (still
       │                                                      │     visible) in regime-aware mode
       │  ⌄  PastCast                                         │
       │    [✓] Hold the map while a loop loads               │  ← PERSISTED, default on (the gate's
       │                                                      │     "Don't hold future loads" turns it off)
       │  ⌄  Radar memory                                     │
       │    This PC        16 GB of RAM   (Use recommended)   │  ← RAM detected; button greys at the default
       │    Radar may use  ────●──────────   4 GB            │  ← PERSISTED (RadarMemoryGb), 1 GB…75% of RAM,
       │    1 pane: 58+ frames  2 panes: 46+  4 panes: 33+    │     default ¼; WORST-case frames per layout
       │    The longest PastCast loop this allows, …          │
       │    Recommended is a quarter of your RAM (4 GB here). │  ← caution colour when High (>½ RAM) / Low
       │  ⌄  Radar site keys                                  │
       │    [✓] Hide the other sites while one is loaded      │  ← PERSISTED, default ON (the `focus` rule)
       │        Click the loaded site again to unload it…     │
       │    [ ] Show only my home and favorite sites          │  ← PERSISTED, default off (the `favorites` rule);
       │        Star sites in the Atlas. The loaded site …    │     the SITE PICKER's footer is the SAME switch;
       │                                                      │     the line says so when there are none
       │    [ ] Show only the sites near the cursor (exp.)    │  ← PERSISTED, default off (the `reveal` rule,
       │        A 230 km ring follows the cursor; …           │     a SITE-REVEAL bolt-on); with favorites on too,
       │                                                      │     favorites always show + the ring adds the rest
       │    The NEXRAD / TDWR / research toggles … still apply│  ← each row = ONE rule in radar-sites.js
       └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

     ⚠️ THE "RANGE RINGS & RULER" SECTION MOVED to its own tab, Radar Range Ring (RangeRingSettingsTab), when
     the rings grew a per-part style editor (2026-09-24). The distance UNIT stayed here: it is app-wide.

     WHY THIS IS NOT IN THE MAP TAB: these are radar CONTENT drawn over the basemap, and they are GLOBAL —
     one copy for the whole map, not one per pane. The Map tab next door owns the basemap and the camera; a
     control that would need a copy per pane belongs in RadarControls instead.

     ⚠️ THE MILE GRID IS GONE, deleted rather than hidden (its VM, its JS module and its IMapService seam
     with it). It drew a square grid anchored to the selected radar as a distance reference, and it did not
     work: at any opacity that made the lines visible over radar returns they were lost in the basemap's own
     lines, and at any opacity that kept them out of the way they were invisible over returns. A distance
     reference wants a different form — range rings from the site, or a point-to-point measure tool — not a
     grid competing with everything already drawn. Don't re-add this one.
     → THAT DIFFERENT FORM NOW EXISTS: the RANGE RULER (Assets/Map/js/radar-ruler.js), armed from the tools
     tier beside the site picker. It draws ONE cased line instead of a field of them, which is the part the
     grid could not do at any opacity. The unit it speaks in is the Readouts section.

     ⚠️ WHY "READOUTS" IS IN THIS TAB and not the Map tab: the Map tab owns the app's LOOK (theme, basemap),
     and a unit is not a look - it is how a RADAR measurement is spoken, and every consumer of it today is a
     radar instrument. ⚠️ GROUND DISTANCES ONLY: heights and wind-profile layer bounds stay in km whatever is
     picked here, because those are meteorological quantities with a conventional unit (Models/Map/DistanceUnits).

     ⚠️ THE TOOLS SECTION IS GONE with the Inspect toggle — Inspect is a MODE you arm and disarm while
     reading the map, not a setting, so it is a key in the OverlayBar now (MainWindow, InspectKey), on the
     bar's left. It is still a MAP tool rather than a per-pane radar control: one armed cursor over a
     shared camera, reading every pane at one point, with only its VALUE readout per-pane (the live tick on
     each pane's product ramp). That reasoning put it in this tab; being a gesture rather than a preference
     is what took it out again.

     ⚠️ THE "RADAR SITES" SECTION IS GONE (2026-09-26). Its Show TDWRs / Show research radars checkboxes became
     two of THREE per-network marker toggles on the tools tier (MapControlsStrip, NEXRAD · TDWR · research), which
     also replaced the old master "show site markers" eye. That ends the old "why is my site gone" hunt across
     two places (the master on the map, the two networks here): every site-marker control is in one place, on
     the map chrome. ⚠️ They are MAP-MARKER toggles
     now — they no longer remove a network from the Atlas or the site picker. Don't re-add a marker control
     here. -->

<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.RadarSettingsTab"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             xmlns:prim="using:Anvil.Controls.Primitives"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <!-- Body: one Primitives/PanelSection per section, grid rows inside each. -->
    <Grid RowSpacing="8" VerticalAlignment="Top">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- home site -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- readouts -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- nowcast live polling -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- pastcast -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- radar memory -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- radar site keys -->
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- The home site is PICKED in the Radar Atlas (where you can see what you're choosing); this only
             shows it and holds the one launch preference. -->
        <prim:PanelSection Grid.Row="0" Header="Home site" IsExpanded="True">
            <!-- ⚠️ "Load home site on launch" MOVED to the Startup tab (2026-10-07) — every launch preference
                 lives there. Don't re-add it here. -->
            <TextBlock Margin="4,0,0,0"
                       Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SiteFavorites.HomeSiteSummary, Mode=OneWay}"
                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <!-- READOUTS - how a measurement is SPOKEN, not what is drawn. One setting so far; it is a section
             rather than a loose row because the next one of its kind (UTC vs local times) lands beside it. -->
        <prim:PanelSection Grid.Row="1" Header="Readouts" IsExpanded="True">
            <Grid RowSpacing="4">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- distance unit -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- what it covers -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Margin="4,0,12,0"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center" Text="Distance"/>

                <!-- A SegmentedPicker, not a ComboBox: three fixed options, and the whole set is worth
                     seeing at once. PERSISTED (AppSettings.DistanceUnits) and pushed into the map page,
                     which formats the ruler's own chip and tick labels itself. -->
                <prim:SegmentedPicker Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1"
                                      HorizontalAlignment="Left" Width="280"
                                      ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.DistanceUnitLabels}"
                                      SelectedIndex="{x:Bind ViewModel.DistanceUnitIndex, Mode=TwoWay}"/>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                           Margin="4,2,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="420"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left" Opacity="0.75"
                           Text="Ground distances - the range ruler's readout and its range labels. Heights and wind-profile levels stay in kilometres."/>
            </Grid>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <!-- NOWCAST LIVE POLLING — when the live poll checks for a new scan (docs/regime-aware-polling.md). REGIME-AWARE
             (default) times each check from the volume's own scan plan (LivePollPlanner); FIXED TIME uses the interval
             row, which stays VISIBLE but greyed in regime-aware mode so you see what switching gives. Both PERSISTED
             (AppSettings.RegimeAwarePolling / LivePollSeconds); a change applies from the next check. -->
        <prim:PanelSection Grid.Row="2" Header="NowCast live polling" IsExpanded="True">
            <StackPanel Spacing="6">
                <prim:SegmentedPicker Margin="4,0,0,0" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Width="280"
                                      ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.LivePollingModeLabels}"
                                      SelectedIndex="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.LivePollingModeIndex, Mode=TwoWay}"/>
                <TextBlock Margin="4,0,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="420"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left" Opacity="0.75"
                           Text="{x:Bind PollingExplainer(ViewModel.Radar.IsFixedTimePolling), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                <Grid ColumnSpacing="12" Margin="4,2,0,0"
                      IsHitTestVisible="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.IsFixedTimePolling, Mode=OneWay}"
                      Opacity="{x:Bind FixedRowOpacity(ViewModel.Radar.IsFixedTimePolling), Mode=OneWay}">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <TextBlock VerticalAlignment="Center" Text="Check every"/>
                    <prim:SegmentedPicker Grid.Column="1" Width="280"
                                          ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.LivePollIntervalLabels}"
                                          SelectedIndex="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.RefreshIntervalIndex, Mode=TwoWay}"/>
                </Grid>
            </StackPanel>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <!-- PASTCAST — the loop holding gate's switch (Composites/LoopHoldingGate). It is also turned off from
             the gate itself ("Don't hold future loads"); this is where it comes back on. -->
        <prim:PanelSection Grid.Row="3" Header="PastCast" IsExpanded="True">
            <!-- PERSISTED (AppSettings.HoldPastCastLoads), default on. -->
            <CheckBox Margin="4,0,0,0"
                      Content="Hold the map while a loop loads"
                      IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.LoopGate.HoldEnabled, Mode=TwoWay}"
                      ToolTipService.ToolTip="Dim the map behind a progress screen until a PastCast loop finishes loading — the map lags while a loop loads"/>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <!-- RADAR MEMORY — the RAM a PastCast loop may hold (Radar.Memory = RadarMemoryViewModel ← Models/RadarMemoryBudget),
             a RAM-allocation slider. PERSISTED (AppSettings.RadarMemoryGb; null = a quarter of RAM). It sizes
             the PastCast frame cap at each Load; NowCast is untouched. The note line swaps to the caution brush when the
             budget is High (over half of RAM) or Low (4-pane loops on the frame floor) — two TextBlocks, never a brush in C#. -->
        <prim:PanelSection Grid.Row="4" Header="Radar memory" IsExpanded="True">
            <Grid RowSpacing="6" ColumnSpacing="12" Margin="4,0,0,0">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- this PC -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- slider -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- frames per layout -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- explainer -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- note / warning -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" VerticalAlignment="Center" Text="This PC"/>
                <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Memory.RamText}"/>
                <Button Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="2" Content="Use recommended" Click="OnUseRecommendedMemoryClick"
                        IsEnabled="{x:Bind Not(ViewModel.Radar.Memory.IsRecommended), Mode=OneWay}"/>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" VerticalAlignment="Center" Text="Radar may use"/>
                <Slider Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Width="220" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        Minimum="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Memory.MinGb}" Maximum="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Memory.MaxGb}"
                        StepFrequency="0.5" SmallChange="0.5" LargeChange="1"
                        IsThumbToolTipEnabled="False"
                        Value="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Memory.BudgetGb, Mode=TwoWay}"/>
                <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="2" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Memory.BudgetText, Mode=OneWay}"/>

                <StackPanel Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="16" Opacity="0.85">
                    <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Memory.OnePaneText, Mode=OneWay}"/>
                    <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Memory.TwoPaneText, Mode=OneWay}"/>
                    <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Memory.FourPaneText, Mode=OneWay}"/>
                </StackPanel>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="420"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left" Opacity="0.75"
                           Text="The longest PastCast loop this allows, counted with every pane showing a different dual-pol product; reflectivity, velocity and SRV panes cost less. NowCast loops always fit."/>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="4" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="420"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left" Opacity="0.75"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind Collapsed(ViewModel.Radar.Memory.IsWarning), Mode=OneWay}"
                           Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Memory.NoteText, Mode=OneWay}"/>
                <TextBlock Grid.Row="4" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="420"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                           Foreground="{ThemeResource SystemFillColorCautionBrush}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind Shown(ViewModel.Radar.Memory.IsWarning), Mode=OneWay}"
                           Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Memory.NoteText, Mode=OneWay}"/>
            </Grid>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <!-- RADAR SITE KEYS — set-once PREFERENCES about how the keys on the map behave, so they pass the placement test for
             Settings (the network toggles are gestures and live on the tools tier — see the ⚠️ above). Each switch is ONE
             rule in radar-sites.js's VISIBILITY RULES table; a new way to hide keys = a rule there + a row here. -->
        <prim:PanelSection Grid.Row="5" Header="Radar site keys" IsExpanded="True">
            <StackPanel Spacing="4">
                <!-- PERSISTED (AppSettings.HideOtherSitesWhileLoaded), default ON — the `focus` rule. -->
                <CheckBox Margin="4,0,0,0"
                          Content="Hide the other sites while one is loaded"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.HideOtherSitesWhileLoaded, Mode=TwoWay}"/>
                <TextBlock Margin="32,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="400"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left" Opacity="0.75"
                           Text="Click the loaded site again to unload it and bring the others back."/>

                <!-- PERSISTED (AppSettings.ShowOnlyFavoriteSites), default off — the `favorites` rule. ⚠️ The SITE PICKER's
                     footer (MapControlsStrip) binds the SAME property: two switches, one value, never a copy. -->
                <CheckBox Margin="4,0,0,0"
                          Content="Show only my home and favorite sites"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.SiteFavorites.ShowOnlyFavoritesOnMap, Mode=TwoWay}"/>
                <TextBlock Margin="32,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="400"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left" Opacity="0.75"
                           Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SiteFavorites.FavoritesOnlyNote, Mode=OneWay}"/>

                <!-- SITE-REVEAL (experimental bolt-on; grep SITE-REVEAL to excise). PERSISTED
                     (AppSettings.RevealSitesNearCursor) — the `reveal` rule. -->
                <CheckBox Margin="4,0,0,0"
                          Content="Show only the sites near the cursor (experimental)"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.RevealSitesNearCursor, Mode=TwoWay}"/>
                <TextBlock Margin="32,0,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="400"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left" Opacity="0.75"
                           Text="A 230 km ring follows the cursor; only the sites inside it show, plus the loaded site."/>
                <!-- end SITE-REVEAL -->

                <TextBlock Margin="4,8,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="420"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left" Opacity="0.75"
                           Text="The NEXRAD / TDWR / research toggles on the tools tier still apply."/>
            </StackPanel>
        </prim:PanelSection>

    </Grid>
</UserControl>
